// Promoted 2026-08-15 from graphix-fuzz/fuzz/crashes/crash_000002.gx,
// one of eight artifacts parked there in June 2026 under the header
// "do not promote to findings/ until fixed (regress runs in-process)".
// They were SIGABRTs — `thread 'tokio-rt-worker' has overflowed its
// stack, fatal runtime error` — and the whole backlog was audited to
// zero on 2026-08-15: every one is now either bounded here or a
// legally-spinning tail loop (design/atomic_recursion.md).
//
// The invariant none of the depth-trip pins stated on its own: an
// UNBOUNDED NON-TAIL recursion must settle on the call-depth limit's
// whole-derivation bottom, never grow the native stack until the
// process aborts. `n - i64:0` never decreases, and `n + f(..)` keeps
// the call live, so this recurses forever at depth; both engines now
// produce an empty trace (bottom) in milliseconds.
//
// A regression here does NOT report as a normal failure — regress runs
// subjects in-process, so a return to stack growth ABORTS the gate
// run. That is loud, if ugly, and was the original reason these sat
// outside the corpus; they are safe to include now that the bound
// holds.
{let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:0, _ => n + f(n - i64:0)}; f(i64:10)}
